oY growth, 50,000 units sold (41% vs 18% industry); Industrial: 22% YoY growth, led by construction (+44%); Aftermarket: 15% YoY growth; International: 37% YoY growth, crossed INR1,000cr gross sales; Financial Services (Arka): AUM up 10% to INR7,947cr, PAT stable at INR69cr","src":"concall","title":"Segment / subsidiary detail"},{"body":"| Challenge | Beneficiary/Loser | Dir | Conviction | Note |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| — | — | — | — | — |","src":"concall","title":"Challenges → beneficiaries & losers"}],"latest_quarter":[{"body":"EBITDA margin expanded 90bps to 13.1% despite commodity inflation; pricing adjustments made periodically but not quantified; operating leverage expected to improve from FY27 as capex ramps and sales scale","src":"concall","title":"Margins & cost dynamics"}],"outlook":[{"body":"revenue growth: targeting $2B by FY30; margin: committed to sustaining 13%+ EBITDA margin; order inflow: not quantified; capex/commissioning: INR1,400cr over FY27-FY28 for 20,000 HHP units at Kagal, with 50,000 unit capacity enhancement (INR700cr) operational by Apr'27","src":"concall","title":"Guidance"},{"body":"not disclosed","src":"concall","title":"Order book & pipeline"},{"body":"HHP segment (up to 6.3MW gensets for NPCIL), data center Edge/Colo/hyperscaler demand, gas/methanol/hydrogen engine readiness, and systems integration via Kirloskar Advanced Systems","src":"concall","title":"Growth verticals / optionality"}]},"sources":["Q4FY26 concall summary","structured quarterly financials","Walk-the-Talk commitments ledger"],"thesis":"KOEL delivered record Q4 standalone sales of INR1,522cr (+24% YoY) and FY26 revenue of INR5,604cr (+25% YoY), driven by 41% volume growth in Powergen (vs 18% industry) and 37% international sales growth, while margin expansion to 13.1% EBITDA margin and INR1,400cr capex for HHP capacity signal structural scaling toward its $2B FY30 target.","track":{"expired_n":0,"open":[],"open_total":0,"quarters_n":0,"revisions":[],"verdicts":[],"